  "criteria": {
    "change_under_test": "the read exit is decided by the anchor count alone: |Anchors_T(q)| = 0 -> no_match, = 1 -> matched, >= 2 -> ambiguous_multiple_anchors.  A query feature with DF = 0 cannot be an anchor, so it lowers the count; it is reported as a reading and cannot short-circuit, weight or bias the exit.  The old early-return path is deleted, not kept as a second criterion.",
    "C1_corpus_frozen_before_run": "the corpus text is written to a snapshot file and its per-paragraph sha256 list is recorded in the manifest before the first reading.  The run reads the snapshot, so editing the plan files afterwards cannot change the acceptance set.",
    "C2_same_implementation_same_switch": "the table under test is the AddressTable allocated by LivingCoreConfig(sc_sfk_enabled=True) through attach_store; writes use write_batch_checked and reads use table.read.  Zero new parameters, zero tensors.",
    "C3_no_threshold_tuning": "no numeric threshold on the read path, no leading margin, no retry with another address definition.  The usable line is fixed at 0.60 in the manifest.",
    "C4_closed_state_neutral": "with the flag at its default the forward pass must reproduce the stored baseline arrays bit for bit (max|delta| = 0), with parameters, state bytes and graph identity unchanged and no table allocated.",
    "V_wrong_pointer": "a should-anchor query answered 'matched' to an address other than its own record",
    "V_anchor_count_unsafe": "wrong_pointer > 0: the no-wrong-answer property depended on rejecting unseen features; go back to the address definition, never tune a threshold.",
    "V_anchor_count_holds": "wrong_pointer = 0 AND usable_ratio >= 0.60 AND the held-out set is 20/20 no_match AND the two-record set is 20/20 ambiguous.  Cost to state: the 'reject on a word never seen' hard guard is gone; false answers are now bounded only by anchor uniqueness and the negative controls.",
    "V_anchor_count_insufficient": "wrong_pointer = 0 AND usable_ratio < 0.60: report the distribution; the line may not be lowered.",
    "V_inconclusive": "wrong_pointer = 0, usable >= 0.60, but a negative control did not hold: report the distribution only.",
    "R_unrelated_reading": "sentences from a file that is never written and is not in the paraphrase table.  A 'matched' answer is counted as a hard answer.  This class is a reading only and never enters the verdict."
  },
  "disclosures": [
    "the exit is the anchor count and nothing else; the DF=0 early return is deleted, so no query is rejected for carrying an unseen word",
    "unseen features are still counted and reported (unknown_features), including their document-frequency histogram, but they never enter the decision",
    "the unrelated set is a reading: a hard answer there is recorded, not scored",
    "the corpus snapshot, not the plan files, is what the run reads, so a later plan edit cannot move the acceptance set",
    "similarity columns are diagnostics; no exit reads them"
